I was just reading some articles and skimmed something about a proposed
EXTRAHARD option.  Seems to me, there's no need for even a HARD option.

Why not just have different difficulty levels which are chosen at the
start?  The game could then have one of:

a different highscore file for each difficulty level
one highscore file but with difficulty level displayed
one highscore file but final score = ending score * difficulty level

1-easy
2-hard
3-extrahard

In order for the difficulty level multiplier idea to be fair, the
bag of holding bug must first be fixed.

Then maybe we hackers could quit bickering about polypiling which
has been impossible to solve because some people want it and some
people don't.  I'd especially like being able to choose a difficulty
when starting because there are some games (when I'm heavy-duty into
nethack) where I prefer not to polypile and some games where the
ability is nice. (like after I haven't played nethack for a month)
For me, it's not even a matter of satisfaction anymore... I've won
so many games I could care less if I polypiled or not.  Rather, it's
a mood thing.  Either I think it's morally ok or I don't, and I've
changed my opinion on that several times in the last few years.
